{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/439505-edimmu-and-the-strix-any-connection","id":439505,"title":"Edimmu and the Strix - Any connection?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-12T23:35:14-07:00","id":439505,"title":"Edimmu and the Strix - Any connection?","content":"Hit me with your theories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T23:48:42-07:00","id":439529,"title":"","content":"<b><i><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&quot;Bah! Our cursed star-cousins have already tasted your form traitor! You are no good to me as a shell! Still, at least I can use to...reproduce easier...&quot;</span></i></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T01:16:35-07:00","id":439600,"title":"","content":"Forgive me, for I am still but a humble Neonate in terms of lore and source material for Vampire: the Requiem. But what are the Edimmu?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T01:50:52-07:00","id":439619,"title":"","content":"Edimmu are sort of like vampire claimed- seven spirits bound together inside a vampire meatsuit (but while corporeal and possessing disciplines, they use spirit rules mostly), they reproduce by being diablorized- each of the seven spirits fly out, one possessing the diablorist, the other six finding new hosts and somehow each bonding with six more spirits.<br /> <br /> Since strix aren't spirits, and the fact that edimmu already have 7 possessing spirits, I'd say good luck to a strix trying to possess one, I'd say no connection whatsoever, why would there be?<br /> <br /> Because they are both different types of ephemerals that possess vampires? <br /> <br /> If I'd connect the edimmu with anything, it would be the idigam. With their abilities of essence shaping, all you'd need is an idigam interested in having vampire servants....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T04:16:21-07:00","id":439715,"title":"","content":"Interesting...<br /> <br /> It's my opinion that the Strix and Kindred are both Vampires but very different and distinct from one another. I know there are a ton of other Vampire creatures that were introduced in the Night Terrors supplements for the gamelines and to some degree they all feed on some fascet of humanity. Be it raw life energy from Vitae or from more metaphysical parts of the human condition like memory.<br /> <br /> It sounds like the Edimmu are more like Spirits that evolved into parasites that reproduce using Vampires as hosts. The Strix may split apart eventualy to &quot;reproduce&quot; themselves but the Owls of Dis primarily concern themselves with growing more powerful and enjoying themselves. The general vibe I got from the book was that they only reproduce at all because their bodies cannot physically contain the power they've accumulated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T09:47:28-07:00","id":440047,"title":"","content":"Can I ask what book/page number the Edimmu can be found in? I've read most of the VtR books and don't remember them. StSword's summary sounds cool, but I'd love to read the description for myself.At a glance it sounds like they have more in common with spirits than Strix.<br /> <br /> Edit: Nevermind, I found them in Ancient Bloodlines, p. 157. I would say there's unlikely to be any connection between the Strix and the Edimmu; Edimmu can only reproduce through diablerie of a vampire, something the Strix don't require at all. In addition the Edimmu have their origins in ancient Babylon, which the Strix supposedly predate. Now, an Edimmu trying to possess a vampire that's already been possessed by a Strix or vice-versa would likely either fail or require a Clash of Wills; I doubt Strix and Edimmu would be able to eat each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2984,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2984-jibkisamabi","user":"JibKisamabi","date":". 03-13-2015, 01:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2984-jibkisamabi","name":"JibKisamabi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T10:06:19-07:00","id":440089,"title":"","content":"They are in Ancient Mysteries book.<br /> What about the connections between Edimmu and Empty Liars from Sacraments and blasphemies? :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1191-rosencroft","name":"Rosencroft","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T22:35:54-07:00","id":440911,"title":"","content":"Personally, I think the Empty Liars are more likely to be a mechanism of the God-Machine than anything spirit related. They have that element of High Strangeness that the God-Machine usually has, they are almost like angels or at least have an element likening them to a Demon's Cover. They stop and observe blood sorcery, they don't try to stop it, they don't prey on the vampire that does it, but if the vampire notices and investigates them they see that their paper trail is flimsy but everyone in their lives will swear up and down they're real. Auspex (used to) reveals them as balloon monsters in the rough shape of people, too. They don't have any supernatural abilities beyond, apparently, their presence altering people's memory to acclimate to their presence. They just keep ticking boxes on some God-Machine infrastructure designed to monitor vampyric activity in a region to ensure their blood sorcery doesn't interfere with Its mechanisms. It does suggest that the God-Machine might be interested in vampires because their patterns of controlling Mortals are in some ways similar to Its own; this would be a way for a storyteller to show that if they wanted to use that idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}